From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypi-for-pwndbg <pwndbg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:59:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dyld cache: 64-bit symtab offsets, skip unknown optional load
 commands

Fixes loading the dylibs of the macOS 27 dyld shared cache:

- All cache dylibs share one __LINKEDIT, up to 0x166168000 bytes past a
  dylib's __TEXT. Once rebased to be relative to the dylib's header (see
  the earlier dyld cache patches), LC_SYMTAB's symoff/stroff no longer
  fit in 32 bits (up to 0x1909e8d00): stroff got truncated, which tripped
  the BFD_ASSERTs in the (un)fixup helpers and made the shared strtab check
  fail ("ffffffff2a884d00 (dylib) != 2a884d00 (ours)"). Make them
  ufile_ptr.
- The target-memory window for a cache dylib was 0xf00db000 bytes, too
  small to reach that __LINKEDIT ("file truncated", and reading the
  indirect symbol table while parsing LC_DYSYMTAB failed, so most dylibs
  were "not in executable format"). Use 16 GiB; memory is read lazily.
- Like dyld, ignore unknown load commands unless LC_REQ_DYLD is set
  (macOS 27 uses 0x37 and 0x3a).
---
 bfd/mach-o.c       | 9 +++++++--
 bfd/mach-o.h       | 7 +++++--
 gdb/solib-darwin.c | 5 ++++-
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bfd/mach-o.c b/bfd/mach-o.c
index cfe68e7..72d77c4 100644
--- a/bfd/mach-o.c
+++ b/bfd/mach-o.c
@@ -3743,7 +3743,7 @@ bfd_mach_o_read_symtab_symbol (bfd *abfd,
   unsigned int wide = mach_o_wide_p (&mdata->header);
   unsigned int symwidth =
     wide ? BFD_MACH_O_NLIST_64_SIZE : BFD_MACH_O_NLIST_SIZE;
-  unsigned int symoff = sym->symoff + (i * symwidth);
+  ufile_ptr symoff = sym->symoff + (i * symwidth);
   struct mach_o_nlist_64_external raw;
   unsigned char type = -1;
   unsigned char section = -1;
@@ -5208,9 +5208,14 @@ bfd_mach_o_read_command (bfd *abfd, bfd_mach_o_load_command *command,
 	return false;
       break;
     default:
+      /* Like dyld, ignore load commands we don't know unless they are
+	 marked as required (LC_REQ_DYLD): newer macOS versions keep adding
+	 them (e.g. 0x37 and 0x3a in the macOS 27 dyld shared cache).  */
+      if (!command->type_required)
+	break;
       command->len = 0;
       _bfd_error_handler (_("%pB: unknown load command %#x"),
-			  abfd, command->type);
+			  abfd, command->type | BFD_MACH_O_LC_REQ_DYLD);
       return false;
     }
 
diff --git a/bfd/mach-o.h b/bfd/mach-o.h
index f2f151c..fa3bac6 100644
--- a/bfd/mach-o.h
+++ b/bfd/mach-o.h
@@ -148,9 +148,12 @@ bfd_mach_o_reloc_info;
 
 typedef struct bfd_mach_o_symtab_command
 {
-  unsigned int symoff;
+  /* 64-bit: for a dylib in the dyld shared cache these are rebased to be
+     relative to the dylib's header, and the cache's shared __LINKEDIT can
+     be more than 4 GiB away from it.  */
+  ufile_ptr symoff;
   unsigned int nsyms;
-  unsigned int stroff;
+  ufile_ptr stroff;
   unsigned int strsize;
   bfd_mach_o_asymbol *symbols;
   char *strtab;
diff --git a/gdb/solib-darwin.c b/gdb/solib-darwin.c
index dca8902..a900c04 100644
--- a/gdb/solib-darwin.c
+++ b/gdb/solib-darwin.c
@@ -709,7 +709,10 @@ darwin_solib_ops::bfd_open (const char *pathname,
        * difficult without constructing this bfd object, which requires that
        * LINKEDIT is within its boundaries. So, for now we resort to this hack
        * where we give the memory view an unfathomable size. */
-      gdb_bfd_ref_ptr res = solib_bfd_open_at (li->lm_addr, 0xf00db000);
+      /* The cache's shared __LINKEDIT can be more than 4 GiB past the
+	 dylib (0x166168000 on macOS 27), so the window must reach it;
+	 memory is only read on demand.  */
+      gdb_bfd_ref_ptr res = solib_bfd_open_at (li->lm_addr, 0x400000000);
       mach_o_data_struct *mdata = bfd_mach_o_get_data (res);
       mdata->dyld_cache_shared
           = get_darwin_info (current_program_space)->dc_shared;
